WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.302
-Republicans are standing
by President Trump,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.070
even after major election losses

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.471
and bombshell testimony

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.440
and, now, they're
calling Democrats dumb.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.542
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.813 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.315
Donald Trump is nothing,

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.250
if not a pioneer
of the English language.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.018
You might think
he's just making up words

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.986
or doesn't know how to read,
but that is not the case.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:22.788
You see,
Trump doesn't make errors.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:23.789
He makes discoveries.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.091
He's like a scholar.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.692
[ Laughter ]
Spends all night scouring

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.962
obscure, 15th-century
medieval texts,

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.863
looking for previously
unknown words.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.398
[as Trump] Eureka!
I found it!

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.167
Lawmakers used to be called...

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.201
-Lawmarkers.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.271
[ Laughter ]
-And, recently, recently,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.306
Dr. Trump has made yet another

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.641
[ Laughter ]
profound linguistic discovery.

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:45.044
He's invented a new,
powerful word

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.079
that he loves so much,
he's now used it twice

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.649
at two different rallies
in the span of one week.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.884
-First, they engineered
the Russia hoax.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.086
That was a total hoax.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:57.089
The single greatest lies

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.458
ever foistered

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.193
[ Laughter ]
upon the American people.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.294
Then, it was Mueller.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:04.564
Remember Mueller,
with that hoax?

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.066
[ Crowd booing ]

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.168
The biggest lie ever foistered

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:10.969
[ Laughter ]
upon the American people.

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:12.338
-That's right, foistered.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.340
[ Laughter ]
He sounds like Daffy Duck

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.642
trying to say "faster."

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.809
[as Daffy] Foister, foister!

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.111
[ Laughter ]
The Democrats are after us!

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:23.248
[ Cheering and applause ]
Trump is surrounded,

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:26.319
surrounded by so many sycophants
that no one was willing

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.987
to tell him
foistered is not a word,

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.522
[ Laughter ]
so he used it twice.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.258
Soon, his underlings are
gonna to start using it, too.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.893
[as official]
This administration is moving

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.496
foister and foister
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.064
than any administration
in history,

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.700
but we're being stonewalled
by Democratic lawmarkers!

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.168
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.838
Trump's not the only linguistic
genius in the GOP this week.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.574
GOP Senator Lindsey Graham
went on Fox News twice

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:49.976
to talk about the
impeachment inquiry.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.178
Now, Graham was asked
about testimony

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.514
from one of Trump's
handpicked ambassadors,

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:55.982
a guy named Gordon Sondland,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.685
who donated $1 million
to Trump's inaugural committee.

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:02.555
This week, Sondland admitted
that there was a quid pro quo

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.757
to get Ukraine
to investigate the company

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.693
that employed Joe Biden's son
Hunter Biden.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.461
That company was called Burisma,

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.995
and, yet,
Graham couldn't pronounce

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.132
either the name Burisma
or the name Sondland.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.534
-There was concern that
the prosecutor was getting

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.036
too close to Hunter Biden,

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.472
that people from Bearmoosa,
whatever the name

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.572
[ Laughter ]
of the company,

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:22.241
a conversation with Sunderland.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.809
Now, here's a question:

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:26.145
Why did Sunderland
change his testimony?

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.414
Was there a connection
between Sunderland

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.883
and Democratic operatives
on the committee?

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.919
It makes me incredil--
incredibly suspicious.

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:37.323
Why did Sunderland
change his mind?

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.358
-You think he's in cahoots
with the Democrats?

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:41.594
You're not even in cahoots
with your own mouth.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.596
[ Laughter ]
Trump and Graham sound like

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.431
two guys leavin' a bar
at 4:00 am,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.099
arguing who should dive home.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:48.167
[as Trump]
Give me the keys.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.702
You're too foistered to drive.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.404
[as Graham] No. Why? No. Why?

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.806
We need a r--
I'll call Sunderland.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.407
[ Laughter and applause ]
He'll pick us up

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:56.943
in his Chevy Buhroozmuh.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.279
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.147
Also, verbal slipups aside,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.449
you think one of Trump's
handpicked ambassadors,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.718
a guy who, again, gave him
$1 million to his campaign,

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.019
is in cahoots
with the Democrats?

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.688
These guys are such
paranoid freaks,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.056
they're gonna start accusing
everyone of bein' against them.

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:12.091
[as Trump]
Who's the whistleblower?

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.092
Is it you, Rudy?

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.426
What's that around your neck?

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:15.495
[as Giuliani]
Oh, no! Oh, no!

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.763
I thought this was
my lucky necklace!

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.264
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.466
And, yet, despite the fact
that these guys can barely get

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.135
two-syllable words
out of their own mouths,

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.236
they're actually accusing
Democrats of being stupid.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.405
Last night, during Trump's
rally in Louisiana,

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:27.639
Senator John Kennedy

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:30.276
brought up the impeachment
inquiry and said this...

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:34.247
-And you know what our Democrats
friends have done for him?!

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:37.483
[ Crowd shouting ]

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:41.286
Speaker Nancy Pelosi
is trying to impeach him!

00:03:41.286 --> 00:03:47.393
[ Booing ]

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.095
I don't mean any disrespect,

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:53.165
but it must suck
to be that dumb!

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:54.567
[ Laughter ]
-I think you did mean

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.369
some disrespect.

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:58.537
I'm sorry, she's dumb?

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.772
You don't get
to call anyone dumb

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:00.873
when you sound like a cross

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.075
between Gomer Pyle
and Foghorn Leghorn.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:06.646
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Scat sings as Kennedy ]

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:09.615
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Continues scat singing ]

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:12.185
[ Cheering ]
I mean, again,

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.653
I don't how can you be
so judgmental.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.522
The dude you're standing next to
thinks foistered is a real word

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.357
[ Laughter ]
and can't even spell

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:20.126
his own name.
That's real.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.293
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:24.229
That is from a tweet
Trump wrote himself.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.065
You know how you get points
on your SATs

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.233
just for writing down your name?

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.701
Trump would be
the first student in history

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.304
to get a score back that said,
"Maybe college isn't for you."

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.339
[ Laughter ]
That same Kennedy's

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.341
also defended Trump
during the impeachment inquiry

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:38.010
by saying that, even if there
was a quid pro quo with Ukraine,

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.845
Trump didn't intend
to break any laws.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:42.248
Kennedy said in an interview,
"To me, it all turns

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.449
on intent motive.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.985
Did the president have
a culpable state of mind?

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.452
Based on the evidence
that I see,

00:04:47.452 --> 00:04:49.789
that I've been allowed to see,
the president does not

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:52.057
have a culpable state of mind."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:54.059
That's because he doesn't
have any state of mind.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:55.628
[ Laughter ]
His mind is empty.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.897
If Trump took a meditation class
and the instructor said,

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.233
"First, begin
by clearing your mind,"

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.501
Trump would immediately shout...

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.335
[as Trump] Done.
I did it. Mind cleared.

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:07.306
[ Laughter ]
Empty head cavern.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.242
So these guys think
there's a shadowy conspiracy

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.943
against them and they
think Democrats are dumb

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.211
for pursuing impeachment,

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.247
despite the fact that a majority
of Americans support it.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.782
In fact, these guys are so
out of touch with reality that,

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.150
when House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.219
first announced the impeachment
inquiry in November,

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.088
Trump himself argued that it
would actually be good for him.

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:26.092
-I just heard
that she'd like to impeach

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.960
and, I mean, if she does that,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.196
they all say that's a positive
for me, from the election.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:33.433
-Oh, do they all say that?

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.100
[ Laughter ]
When you say they, do you mean

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.503
your other personalities?
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:38.771
[as Trump] Scared Trump
says it's bad.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.339
Sassy Trump says it's good

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.575
and Nerdy Trump says bazinga.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.109
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.978
So Trump said impeachment
would actually be good

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.980
for him politically
and, yet, on Tuesday,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.082
Republicans saw major losses
in Virginia;

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.918
and Kentucky, where a Democrat
won the governor's race

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.620
in a state Trump won
by 30 points.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.256
Now, to be clear, Kentucky's
incumbent Republican governor,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.092
Matt Bevin, was one of the most

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.459
unpopular governors
in the country.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:02.628
He fought with teachers
and tried to gut Medicaid.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.465
Overturned an executive order
restoring felon voting rights

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.399
and he tried to implement
work requirements

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:08.701
for Medicaid recipients.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.869
And I would just like to say,
if we're gonna start

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:13.706
instituting work requirements
for federal programs,

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.240
maybe we should start
with the presidency.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.143
I mean, Trump is always golfing.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:20.012
He never works. He's like
that friend everyone has

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.715
who's always posting photos
from exotic locations,

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.350
but when you ask him what he
does for a living, he's like,

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.852
"Uh, well, I'm workin' on an app
that tells you

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:28.287
which Starbucks
has the best bathrooms.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.788
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, it's called --

00:06:29.788 --> 00:06:30.989
it's called Starbutts.

00:06:30.989 --> 00:06:33.626
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:36.495
So Bevin's defeat --
[ Applause ]

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:38.463
Bevin's defeat was a rejection,
not just of Trump,

00:06:38.463 --> 00:06:41.867
but of the GOP agenda on issues
like healthcare and education.

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:44.002
But the race was also
very much about impeachment.

00:06:44.002 --> 00:06:47.039
In fact, a source close
to Trump even admitted

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:49.375
the GOP losses on Tuesday
were a bad sign,

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.043
both for Trump's
reelection campaign

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.511
and the impeachment inquiry.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.613
-A source close
to the White House told CNN

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:56.315
the results were totally bad.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.550
Kentucky and Virginia
signaled to the GOP

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:01.553
they are underestimating
voter intensity against Trump

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:04.089
and it could be terrible
for them next year.

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:05.891
Bad omen for impeachment.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:07.359
-You guys really needed an omen

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:09.195
to tell you things
were not looking good?

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:11.497
[ Laughter ]
Republicans are like
Ancient Egyptians

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:12.631
trying to predict the seasons.

00:07:12.631 --> 00:07:14.066
"The air is cooling.
What could it mean?

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.903
We must look to the stars
for a sign."

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:19.372
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:20.706
Ammit.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.141
And, what's worse --
[ Applause ]

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.709
what's worse for Republicans

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.277
is they have
no credible defense.

00:07:25.277 --> 00:07:27.079
They're flailing.
In fact, yesterday,

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.681
an MSNBC reporter caught up

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.382
to Republican
Congressman Mark Meadows,

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:31.984
a staunch Trump ally.

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:34.053
Meadows was desperate to prove
that Republicans

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.854
were not losing
the impeachment fight.

00:07:35.854 --> 00:07:37.489
-Hold on.
We have Mark Meadows right here.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:39.124
Congressman Meadows,
can we talk live?

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:41.927
So he's walking by right now,
but Republicans

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:43.396
are really struggling
to defend

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:44.963
-I'll talk to you.
-the president -- Okay. Great.

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:46.098
-We're not struggling
on anything.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.532
-Okay, so Congressman --
-So, the Republicans

00:07:47.532 --> 00:07:49.034
are not struggling on anything.

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:51.904
[ Laughter ]
-He's like a guy who's too proud

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.306
to admit he doesn't
know how to swim.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:54.306
[as Meadows]
I'm not drownin'.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:56.475
Do not throw me
a life preserver.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:57.909
I love the taste of salt water.

00:07:57.909 --> 00:07:59.679
I think I can see
my grandmother.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:01.847
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.817
Also, can we hear that clip
again, with the tire screeching?

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.551
-Congressman Meadows,
can we talk live?

00:08:06.551 --> 00:08:09.421
So he's walking by right now,
but Republicans

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:11.123
are really struggling to defend
[ Tire screeches ]

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.658
[ Laughter ]
the president -- Okay. Great.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.226
-Struggling on anything.
-Okay.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:16.295
-And, now,
[ Applause ]

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.230
[ Cheering ]
even Trump's own appointees --

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.765
[ Applause ]

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:21.333
Trump's own appointees
are admitting

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.535
there was a quid pro quo
with Ukraine,

00:08:23.535 --> 00:08:25.738
so Republicans are changing
their argument again.

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:28.073
Yesterday, Lindsey Graham,
the guy who couldn't even

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:29.741
pronounce the name
of one of the key witnesses,

00:08:29.741 --> 00:08:31.510
said Trump couldn't
have orchestrated

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.513
a quid pro quo with Ukraine
because he is too incompetent.

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:37.216
-What I can tell you about the
Trump policy toward the Ukraine:

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.450
It was incoherent.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.386
It depends on who you talk to.

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:43.255
They seem to be incapable
of forming a quid pro quo.

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:45.624
-So they can't be criminals
because they're stupid.

00:08:45.624 --> 00:08:48.093
[ Laughter ]
It is not good when your defense

00:08:48.093 --> 00:08:49.662
is also a confession.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:51.296
No version of that is good.

00:08:51.296 --> 00:08:52.698
Either they broke the law
or they're morons.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.366
It's like if a cop
pulled you over and said,

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:55.834
"Do you know the speed limit?"

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.270
And you responded,
"Of course not.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.571
I'm too drunk to read the sign."

00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:00.105
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.105 --> 00:09:01.607
So I guess what Graham
is saying is

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.776
they would have committed
the crime, but they were too...

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.011
-Dumb!

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:07.246
[ Laughter ]
-This week should put to rest

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:09.415
any speculation that impeachment
should somehow help trump.

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:11.683
It should also reminds us
that the GOP agenda,

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:14.653
on issues like healthcare,
education, and voting rights,

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:15.687
is deeply unpopular.

